{"id":"resp_b4bf1607eb706b5a","created_at":1795617831,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9ad14a05f99c4631","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shape capturing requirement: \"All welding within ice-strengthened areas is to be of the double continuous type.\"\n\nWe have ontology: ship, weld, hasWeld (ship -> weld), weldType (weld -> weldTypeValue), doubleContinuousWeld is a NamedIndividual of weldTypeValue.\n\nAlso property withinIceStrengthenedArea: domain weld (owner is weld per termOwners) and range boolean indicating if the weld is within ice-strengthened area? Actually termOwners says withinIceStrengthenedArea owned by weld. So weld has property withinIceStrengthenedArea (boolean). Need to enforce that for any weld that has withinIceStrengthenedArea true, the weld's weldType must be doubleContinuousWeld.\n\nAlso iceStrengthenedArea property is for benchmarkEntity, but not needed.\n\nWe must not invent target selectors beyond admitted population: admission says focus_set mode COMPLETE_CLASS_POPULATION_PER_INPUT owner_class ship. So target class ship population. So SHACL shapes: a shape for ship? Perhaps node shape targeting ship, with property shapes linking to welds via hasWeld, then constraints on those weld nodes.\n\nSimplify: create a shape ex:WeldShape targeting weld class, with property path withinIceStrengthenedArea = true (value true) then requires weldType value equal to doubleContinuousWeld. In SHACL, we can use sh:property with sh:path, sh:hasValue for boolean true, and sh:qualifiedValueShape + sh:qualifiedMinCount. For weldType constraint: we need that when withinIceStrengthenedArea true, weldType must have value doubleContinuousWeld. Use sh:if? There is sh:condition? Not standard. Use sh:property with sh:path having a sh:hasValue true for withinIceStrengthenedArea, and then sh:qualifiedValueShape linking to weldType? Actually could use sh:or with a shape that either withinIceStrengthenedArea false or weldType is doubleContinuousWeld. Since requirement means \"if withinIceStrengthenedArea then doubleContinuous\". So we can express as sh:property with sh:path withinIceStrengthenedArea, sh:hasValue true, sh:message... and a sh:property for weldType with sh:in containing doubleContinuousWeld but only when previous is true; but SHACL does not have conditional. Could use sh:nodeKind sh:IRI and sh:in.\n\nAlternative: use sh:rule? But simpler: define a shape that requires that for any weld, either withinIceStrengthenedArea false or weldType is doubleContinuousWeld. Use sh:property with sh:path [sh:or...]? There is sh:or to allow alternatives for the whole node. We can define sh:or with two node shapes: one where withinIceStrengthenedArea false, another where weldType is doubleContinuousWeld. So shape ex:WeldRequirementShape with sh:or [ { sh:property [ sh:path withinIceStrengthenedArea ; sh:hasValue false ] } , { sh:property [ sh:path weldType ; sh:hasValue <doubleContinuousWeld> ] } ].\n\nBut must ensure both conditions are satisfied? Actually need both present? The or allows either, which is correct: either not within area, or correct type.\n\nWill need prefixes.\n\nAlso need target for ship? Could have shape ex:ShipWeldShape targeting ship, requiring that hasWeld points to nodes that satisfy ex:WeldRequirementShape via sh:property sh:qualifiedValueShape? Use sh:property path hasWeld, sh:qualifiedValueShape ex:WeldRequirementShape, sh:qualifiedMinCount 0 (or maybe 0?). Actually need to enforce for each weld. Use sh:property with sh:path hasWeld, sh:node ex:WeldRequirementShape.\n\nSimpler: direct shape for weld class enough, but target ship population might be required by admission. We'll include both: ship target shape linking to weld shape.\n\nImplement shapes:\n\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>.\n@prefix ex: <http://example.org/shacl#>.\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>.\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.\n\nex:WeldRequirementShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass vocab:weld; sh:or ( [ sh:property [ sh:path vocab:withinIceStrengthenedArea ; sh:hasValue false ; sh:datatype xsd:boolean ] ] [ sh:property [ sh:path vocab:weldType ; sh:hasValue vocab:doubleContinuousWeld ; sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ] ] ) .\n\nex:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass vocab:ship; sh:property [ sh:path vocab:hasWeld ; sh:node ex:WeldRequirementShape ] .\n\nAdd messages.\n\nNo invented owners, done.\n\nReturn BEGIN_SHACL and END_SHACL.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_93a33382a15950f9","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix ex: <http://example.org/shacl#> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that captures the welding requirement for weld entities.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:WeldRequirementShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:weld ;\n    ## Requirement: if a weld is within an ice‑strengthened area,\n    ## then its weld type must be the double continuous weld.\n    ## Expressed as: ( NOT withinIceStrengthenedArea ) OR ( weldType = doubleContinuousWeld )\n    sh:or (\n        # Case 1 – the weld is **not** within an ice‑strengthened area.\n        [\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:withinIceStrengthenedArea ;\n                sh:hasValue false ;\n                sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;\n                sh:message \"Weld is not within an ice‑strengthened area.\" ;\n            ] ;\n        ]\n        # Case 2 – the weld is within an ice‑strengthened area and must be double‑continuous.\n        [\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:weldType ;\n                sh:hasValue vocab:doubleContinuousWeld ;\n                sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;\n                sh:message \"Weld within ice‑strengthened area must be of type double continuous.\" ;\n            ] ;\n        ]\n    ) ;\n    sh:message \"Weld does not satisfy the double‑continuous requirement for ice‑strengthened areas.\" .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Ship shape that links ships to their welds and enforces the weld\n# requirement on each associated weld.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:hasWeld ;\n        sh:node ex:WeldRequirementShape ;\n        sh:message \"Associated weld must satisfy the double‑continuous requirement when positioned in ice‑strengthened areas.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:message \"Ship has welds that violate the double‑continuous welding rule for ice‑strengthened areas.\" .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":15173,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":14576,"input_tokens_per_turn":[15173],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1534,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1033,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1534],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":16707},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}